/**
 * Unit-test configuration. This file exists so `npm test` can never reach a real
 * D1 database.
 *
 * ## Why this file has to exist
 *
 * The unit test config used to read `wrangler.jsonc`, which is the *production*
 * configuration: it names the production database (`campus-flow-db`,
 * `814ad3eb-0811-4fa2-86a3-953de59dcf5e`) and sets `"remote": true` on the `DB`
 * binding. That combination is not safe under `@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`, and the
 * reason is worth writing down because it is not obvious:
 *
 *   1. The plugin's pool options schema declares `remoteBindings: z.boolean()
 *      .default(true)`. A config that does not mention it still gets `true`.
 *   2. With `remoteBindings` on, the pool collects "remote" bindings via
 *      `pickRemoteBindings`, which selects any binding where
 *      `"remote" in binding && binding.remote`. `"remote": true` on the D1 binding
 *      qualifies.
 *   3. A non-empty selection makes the pool open a genuine remote dev session
 *      (`startRemoteProxySession`) against the Cloudflare API using that binding's
 *      `database_id`.
 *   4. `d1DatabaseEntry` only routes a binding through that proxy when *both* a
 *      connection string and `remote` are present -- which is exactly the case
 *      here.
 *
 * So `npm test` would have opened the production database, and `tableResolver.spec.ts`
 * contains `DROP TABLE IF EXISTS`, `DELETE FROM academic_batches` and
 * `DROP TABLE academic_batches`. Whether that failed loudly or destroyed real data
 * came down to whether a remote session could be authenticated -- not a safe
 * default.
 *
 * ## What this file guarantees
 *
 * No `remote` key, so `pickRemoteBindings` finds nothing, no remote session is
 * opened, `d1DatabaseEntry` returns a local `{ id }`, and the pool serves D1 from
 * Miniflare's isolated per-test-file storage under `.wrangler/state/`.
 *
 * The `database_id` is a placeholder in the all-zeroes test range. It is only ever
 * used as a local storage key, and it cannot resolve to a real Cloudflare database,
 * so pointing this binding at production would require deliberately typing the
 * production id here.
 *
 * `remoteBindings: false` is also set explicitly in `vitest.config.mts` and
 * `vitest.integration.config.mts`, so that a future `"remote": true` added to this
 * file still cannot open a proxy session.
 *
 * This file must never be used by `wrangler dev` or `wrangler deploy`.
 */
{
	"$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
	"name": "campus-flow-unit-tests",
	"main": "src/index.ts",
	"compatibility_date": "2026-09-21",
	"d1_databases": [
		{
			"binding": "DB",
			"database_name": "campus-flow-unit-tests",
			"database_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002"
		}
	],
	"vars": {
		"NODE_ENV": "test",
		"ALLOWED_ORIGINS": "http://localhost:5173"
	}
}